@obverse
1. {d}a-nu ir-hi-a-am ša-me-e ša-mu-u₂ er-ṣe-tam ul-d[u-n]im
#tr.en: Anu begot the sky, the sky bore the earth,
2. er-ṣe-tum u₂-li-id bu-ša-am bu-šum u₂-li-id lu-hu-ma-a-am
#tr.en: The earth bore the stench, the stench bore the mud,
3. lu-hu-mu-um u₂-li-id zu!-ba! zu!-u[b]-bu u₂-li-id tu-ul-tam
#tr.en: The mud bore the fly, the fly bore the “worm”.
4. tu-ul-tum DUMU!.SAL! {d}gu-la lu-ul-lu-um-tam lu-ub-bu-ša-at da-mi ha-ab-ra-at
#tr.en: The “worm”, the daughter of Gula, is clad in a l.-garment, thick with blood,
5. a-ak?#-[ki?]-lu da-mi ṣe-eh-ri-im u₂-pe₂-el-li-a-am i-ni-i-šu
#tr.en: The de[vour]er of the child’s blood is reddening his eyes.
6. id-di# ši#-ip#-tam# {d}da#-mu# u₃# {d}gu#-la# u₂-ni-ra tu#-ul#-tam# [e?-bi?]-tam?# | iṭ-bu-uh-šu-nu#-ti# a-na ṣ[e?]-eh?!-r[i?-im?]
#tr.en: Damu cast the incantation and Gula slew the [thi]ck “worm”, slaughtered them for the (sake of the) c[hil]d,
7. ip-te pi₂-i-šu iṣ-ṣa-bat tu-la-a-am iš-ši-i-ma i-ni-šu i-[ni?-iq?]
#tr.en: He opened his mouth, took the (mother’s) breast, raised his eyes, (began to) s[uck].
8. ši-ip-tum u₂-ul ia-a-tum ši-pa-at {d}da-mu u₃ {d}gu-la {d}d[a-m]u [i]d-di-ma a-na-ku el-qe₂
#tr.en: The incantation is not mine, (it is) the incantation of Damu and Gula. Damu cast (it) and I took (it). 
9. i-nu-ma {d}gu-la il-li-ku mu-tu-tam kal-bu il-li-ku wa-ar-ki-i-ša
#tr.en: When Gula was walking in bravery, (her) dogs were walking behind her.
10. tu-li-a-tum i-dam ia-ši-im su-up-pu u₃ ṣu₂-hu-um ša il-li-ku wa-ar-ki-ša i-[n]u-ma {d}EN.ZU iš-tu NIBRU{ki} u₂-ṣi-a-am
#tr.en: - “Worms ! to (my) side ! to me !” Prayer(s) and Laughter that were walking behind her. When Sîn came out of Nippur he released
11. u₂-wa-aš-še-e[r zu? | ku?-u]b-ba-am u₃ GIR₂.TAB a-na qa₂-aq-qa₂-di-im m[u!-n]am! a-na ap-pi₂ ṣe-eh-ri-im be₂-li it-ta-di
#tr.en: the [fly( ?)/ee]l( ?) and the scorpion to the head. My lord threw the larva to the child’s nose.
12. ṣe-eh-rum la i-de-a-am mu-ru-us-su la i-de-a-am ta-ni-hi-šu ta#-az#-zi-qi₂-šu
#tr.en: May the child not experience (any more of) his illness, may he not experience (any more of) his distress, (of) his anxiety !
13. ak-nu-uk ap-pa-am u₃ ha-si₂-sa₃-am ak-nu-uk ši-pi-a-tim ša mu-hi-i-šu ša al-la-tum i-ra-am-mu-šu
#tr.en: I have sealed (his) nose and (his) ear. I have sealed the sutures of his skull that Allatum has loosened.
14. i-di-a-am a-na bi-ri-tu tu-li-ša ši-ip-tum u₂-ul ia-a-tum ši-pa-at {d}gu-la
#tr.en: She threw (him ? it ?) in between her breast. This incantation is not mine : (it is) the incantation of Gula.
27. as-ku-up-pa-tum šu-te-ri-bi ma-re-e-ki
#tr.en: O threshold! keep letting your sons enter!
28. {d}asar-lu₂-hi DUMU {d}en-ki i-ir-ru-ba-am
#tr.en: Asarluhi the son of Enki is entering.